\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Qualitative comparison of anti-correlated failure modes. Top row: a high-instability case (mean Dice~=~0.68, gap~=~0.52). The six single-reference predictions vary substantially in quality but all capture the nucleus region. Bottom row: a high-catastrophic case (mean Dice~=~0.03, gap~=~0.04). All six predictions fail, with near-zero variance across references. The anti-correlation is visually evident: high variance implies non-catastrophic, low variance implies catastrophic.}}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:qualitative}{{3}{5}{}{figure.3}{}}
